---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---
<Base title="About" description="About Courtney Root, security engineer focused on AI and cloud security.">
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <div class="about-intro">
    <img src="/headshot.webp" alt="Courtney Root" width="240" height="240" class="headshot" />
    <div>
      <h1>Hi, I'm Courtney.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I'm a cybersecurity engineer with four years securing cloud products used by customers at scale.
        These days I spend most of my time thinking about what AI changes for attackers, defenders, and
        the people who have to decide what to fund.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>
    I hold a Master of Cybersecurity from Georgia Tech, where I studied everything from incident response
    to cyber deterrence policy. Now I'm finishing an MBA at UC Berkeley's Haas School of Business (Class of 2027),
    which is where the "security as a business decision" thread in my writing comes from.
  </p>
  <p>
    I'm a big believer in capture-the-flag events as an on-ramp into the field, and I give back by reviewing talk submissions for the Women in Cybersecurity (WiCyS) 2027 conference.
  </p>

  <h2 id="bios">Bios for organizers</h2>
  <h3>Short</h3>
  <blockquote>
    Courtney Root is a cybersecurity engineer focused on AI and cloud security, and an MBA candidate at UC Berkeley Haas.
  </blockquote>
  <h3>Long</h3>
  <blockquote>
    Courtney Root is a cybersecurity engineer with four years of experience securing cloud products for customers.
    Courtney's work and writing focus on securing AI systems, using AI to strengthen defense, and translating
    security risk for business leaders. Courtney holds a Master of Cybersecurity from Georgia Tech, is completing
    an MBA at UC Berkeley's Haas School of Business (Class of 2027), and serves as a program reviewer for the
    WiCyS 2027 conference.
  </blockquote>
  <p class="muted">A high-resolution headshot is available <a href="/og-image.jpg">here</a>.</p>

  <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={SITE.links.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a></li>
    <li><a href={SITE.links.github}>GitHub</a></li>
    <li><a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></li>
  </ul>
</Base>
